; The miss: `u_tim` is one letter short of the extracted `u_time`, so
; the last bind fires `not_cross_ref` — the same code and the same
; `[bind, uniform]` slot path an identity-route miss produces, because
; from the reference side nothing is different.
;
; The message names `:src`, not `:name`, and that is the repair route:
; the legal names live *inside the string*, so either reference one that
; is already there or add a `var<uniform>` declaration to the WGSL.
; Adding `(shader :name u_tim …)` registers nothing — it declares a
; shader, not a uniform.
(use-plugin "uniforms")

(shader :name sky :src """@group(0) @binding(0) var<uniform> u_time: f32;
@group(0) @binding(1) var<uniform> u_resolution: vec2f;
""")

(bind :uniform u_resolution :group 0 :binding 1)
(bind :uniform u_tim :group 0 :binding 0)
